+# VisitSheet rc4 acceptance contract
+
+Goal: ship a local candidate `rc4` on top of `rc3` (`b807fc514795b52b52715879e8e85699bb219327`) that restores the large-text floor and points the delivery records at the Bailian narrated demo. The product still follows `idea.md`. Where `prd.md` or `qa.md` disagree, `idea.md` wins (one fictional account, dates counted from the login day, a private sandbox per login, Display works before login).
+
+This round does not deploy, push, or submit.
+
+## Core flows that must still close
+
+1. Login with **Fill in the demo login** (`demo@visitsheet.example` / `demo-pass-48`) creates a private sandbox. The dashboard shows the next visit in 7 days.
+2. **Make my brief** shows the access card, the top-three box, notes, medicines, and the disclaimer. Print preview of the normal brief is one Letter page and one A4 page. The large-print brief is two Letter pages and two A4 pages.
+3. On the visit, **Up** moves a question into the top three. **Add to this visit** carries over an unasked question from the earlier visit.
+4. **Display** saves large text and high contrast in the `vs_display` cookie. The choice applies before login and remains after logout.
+5. Error paths still render the app error page with the disclaimer and no stack or filesystem path: empty login, wrong password, 404, 403, 413, 415.
+
+## Environment
+
+- Workspace: `/workspace/visit-sheet-rc3`
+- Node.js 22 LTS (`/tmp/node22/node_modules/node/bin/node`, v22.x). System Node 20 cannot load the local `better-sqlite3` binary.
+- Start: `npm install && npm run seed && npm start` (optional `PORT`, default 3000).
+- Browser evidence: headless Chrome via Playwright. No paid API.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope:
+
+- Large-text CSS in `public/css/app.css` so visible text stays at least 22px and headings stay larger than body text.
+- A font-size and overflow scan in the committed verifier.
+- Reshoot screenshots `01` and `08` after that CSS fix.
+- Docs and BUILD records for `/workspace/demo/visit-sheet-demo-v4.mp4`.
+- Node 22 `npm test`, full verifier, PDF page counts, `BUILD-RC4.txt`, local commit and tag `rc4`, and `review/rc4/` evidence.
+
+Out of scope:
+
+- Re-recording the demo video.
+- Push, cloud deploy, Devpost submit, public GitHub URL.
+- Optional items from the rc3 review (future-visit carry, iOS dates, auto-submit Asked, duplicate button names, checkbox size, README env vars, wide layout, screen readers, other browsers).
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+A1. With the `vs_display=large` cookie, every visible text node on every walked page renders at 22px or larger. Exclude `.visually-hidden` and `.sr-only`. This includes the login demo email and password (`.mono`), including at a viewport of 480px or narrower, where `.mono` is currently forced to 14px.
+
+A2. In large-text mode, `h2` and `h3`, and the links inside them, render larger than body text (strictly greater than 22px). Medicine-card titles (`h3.med-line`) are included. Title links on the dashboard are included.
+
+A3. In large-text mode, the large-print brief header (brand, navigation, Log out) renders at 22px or larger. Wrapping is allowed. There is no horizontal overflow. Large-print without the large-text cookie may keep the 18px header.
+
+A4. Print output is unchanged: `pdfinfo` reports Letter and A4 normal brief = 1 page each, large-print = 2 pages each (1/1/2/2). The normal Letter PDF still contains the disclaimer and does not contain "Log out".
+
+A5. `scripts/verify.py` (adapted from `/tmp/vs-demo/verify.py`) sets `vs_display=large`, walks these 13 pages, and asserts A1–A3 plus no horizontal overflow at 320, 390, and 1440:
+
+1. `/login`
+2. `/about`
+3. `/display`
+4. `/dashboard`
+5. `/visits/<next visit id>`
+6. `/visits/<next>/brief`
+7. `/visits/<next>/brief?text=large`
+8. `/medicines`
+9. `/about-me`
+10. `/settings`
+11. `/visits/<next>/delete`
+12. `/demo/reset`
+13. `/no-such-page`
+
+The script also keeps the existing rc3 checks (health, 404, 413, 415, judge path, keyboard edit, carry, cross-sandbox, print sizes). Full run: 0 failures. Results record the minimum font size and the selector that produced it.
+
+A6. `docs/screenshots/01-login.png` and `docs/screenshots/08-high-contrast.png` are reshot after the CSS fix. `01` is the login page in large-text mode with the fictional demo credentials visible. `08` is large text plus high contrast (dashboard, same crop as before: above "New visit").
+
+A7. `docs/devpost.md` Demo video section and the BUILD records name `/workspace/demo/visit-sheet-demo-v4.mp4` as the delivery video, with measured facts:
+
+- sha256 `33dada6c472fe69d7a6d363407e513e3239d6042ebc4af7ae02548d529e5e5be`
+- duration about 157.95 s (about 2:38)
+- 1920×1080 H.264 at 30 fps
+- video stream bit-identical to v2; video-stream sha256 `910a8fb974a30c9080e5dc7c5fa92b1418c26cb233001b993467154aabf41b93`
+- audio AAC LC stereo 48 kHz, about 136 kbps
+- TTS: DashScope / Bailian, model `qwen3-tts-flash`, voice `Cherry`
+
+The repo must not tell a reader that the delivery demo is silent `visit-sheet-demo-v2.mp4`. v2 may be mentioned only as the older picture-identical file.
+
+A8. Because the video is not re-recorded, the docs and `BUILD-RC4.txt` state that timestamps about 134–149 s still show the pre-fix large-text sizes.
+
+A9. `npm test` is run with Node 22. Raw output is saved and shows a pass.
+
+A10. Evidence file mtimes (`review/rc4/evidence/` results, test log, pdfinfo, reshot screenshots) are later than the last product change (`public/css/app.css` and `scripts/verify.py`).
+
+A11. `BUILD-RC4.txt` records the start command, port, Node version, A1–A11 pass/fail with evidence paths, and the demo v4 sha256, duration, audio, and TTS facts.
+
+A12. Local commit on the worktree branch, annotated tag `rc4` on that commit, worktree clean. No git push, no new remote, no Devpost action.
+
+A13. `review/rc4/` contains the original requirements pointer, source hash, diff from rc3, start command, per-item acceptance table, run evidence, and known issues.
+
+## Known issues carried forward
+
+No public URL, no GitHub remote, MemoryStore sessions, Asked still auto-submits, README mentions only `PORT`, print is black text, checked in headless Chrome only, `qa.md` still names the older sample account, the demo subtitle bar covers the bottom 150px, and the v4 picture at about 134–149 s predates the large-text fix.
